  "body": "**Stacked on #1025 (on #975, #964).** This branch was cut from `issue/1011-lathe-cycle-exit`, so until those three merge, its diff also shows their commits. Merge order: #964, #975, #1025, then this one. Only the top commit, `fix(post): the Fanuc lathe seats an off-seat face cycle by the hop law`, belongs to this PR.\n\n## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` now uses #994's `cycleSeat`. A face cycle (G83/G84/G85) is read with the tool on centre at R. When the cycle record arrives with the tool somewhere else, the post seats it with the hop law:\n\n1. If the tool is below R, `G00 Z<R>` first (out of the work).\n2. If it is off centre, `G00 X0` (onto the centre at the safe level).\n3. If it is above R, `G00 Z<R>` (down to the seat).\n\nThis replaces the old single `G00 X0 Z<R>`, which was one diagonal X+Z rapid. If a group is still open, `G80` is written before the seat moves.\n\n**Axis assumption.** \"Away from the work\" is +Z. That is the post's own Z law: Z runs along the spindle axis with the face at the free end, face cycles drill toward -Z from R, and #1011's `onHole` (`Z <= R`) already relies on it. It also matches the usual public lathe G-code convention, where Z+ points away from the chuck and the face. The post does not just assume this: it checks the record's bottom is below its R.\n\n**Refused by name, no cycle written.** These cycles cannot be seated:\n- the cycle is its section's first motion, so there is no stream position to seat from (\"approach the hole first\");\n- the record's bottom is not below its R (\"cannot tell which way is clear of the face\");\n- a legacy record has no R and starts off the axis.\n\n**tormach-lathe** is unchanged. It writes no cycle and no positioning block of its own. A new pin shows that every motion line it posts is one of the stream's moves, in order.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1026-lathe-cycle-seat.md`.\n\n### Before / after\n\nThe synthetic stream reads the cycle at radius 15, Z18, with R22, bottom 10 and exit 40.\n\nBefore (parent's .cps):\n```\nG00 X30 Z18\nG00 X0 Z22        <- one X+Z rapid, below R toward the face\nG83 Z10 F0.1\nG80\nG00 X0 Z40\n```\nAfter:\n```\nG00 X30 Z18\nG00 Z22\nG00 X0\nG83 Z10 F0.1\nG80\nG00 X0 Z40\n```\nFrom above R (X30 Z30), the order is `G00 X0` then `G00 Z22`.\n\n## Tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/lathe_cycle_exit.rs`:\n- The #1011 read-back checker now also reads the seat. Before the hole, a move that changes X from a known position must stay at Z >= R, and the face cycle must be read on X0 at R.\n- New tests:\n  - `fanuc_lathe_seats_an_off_seat_face_cycle_by_the_hop_law`: below R and above R, both off centre.\n  - `fanuc_lathe_refuses_a_face_cycle_it_cannot_seat_by_name`: a first-motion cycle, and R below the bottom.\n  - `tormach_lathe_adds_no_positioning_move_to_an_off_seat_face_cycle`.\n  - `the_checker_catches_an_off_seat_cycle_reached_by_one_diagonal`.\n- The existing `both_lathe_posts_leave_a_face_drilled_hole_at_the_streams_exit` runs with the seat check on both posts and still passes.\n\n`crates/app/tests/lathe_post_refusals.rs`: two synthetic fixtures read the cycle as the section's first motion, which is now refused. They gain the approach rapid that the generator's streams carry, and their assertions are unchanged:\n- `a_face_cycle_ends_on_the_rapid_leaving_its_hole_and_refuses_a_cut_that_leaves`\n- `a_section_without_surface_speed_posts_g97_after_one_with_it`\n\n**Revert check.** With the parent's `fanuc-lathe.cps` put back, both fanuc tests fail. The seat test fails with ``line 11: `G00 X0 Z22` moves X at Z18, below the seat Z22``, and the refusal test fails because no refusal is raised. The checker and tormach tests pass either way.\n\n**Goldens.** No golden moved. The axial-drill stream approaches R on centre before its cycle, so `golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/axial_drill.nc` is unchanged (`lathe_post` and `golden_cl` are green).\n\n**Gate.** `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green (1 step, every app suite the stack touches, 25.3 min, 0 failed). By hand: lathe_cycle_exit, lathe_post, lathe_post_refusals, lathe_post_g76, lathe_post_tormach, drilling_axial, posting, golden_cl, conformance and c_axis_live, plus the other suites that post on fanuc-lathe (lathe_spindle_law, program_entry, c_axis_unwind, wear_comp, lathe_blade_corner, comment_escape, coolant_followups, control_comp, lathe_nose_tip, inverted_post, turning_face_approach, drill_prior, drill_prior_kinds) and camcraft-post `comp`: all green (23 app binaries + post `comp`); clippy `-D warnings` clean on the two touched test binaries.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real control or simulator run of the seated sequence.\n- No G84/G85 off-seat stream. Their seating takes the same path as G83 (the seat code does not depend on the cycle word).\n- No stream with an inverted Z machine axis. `invert::apply` mirrors the stream before the post, and no shipped lathe states one.\n\nChangelog: The Fanuc lathe post seats a face cycle read off its hole by the hop law (Z out to R, onto the centre, down), never one diagonal rapid; one it cannot seat is refused by name (#1026)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nFixes #1026\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
